dy's exploring sexuality um  increasingly gender all other all kinds  of other aspects of of um  their identity  and schools have to stay on top of that  so they do have to handle children with  gender identity issues sensitively but  um safeguarding children and biological  sex absolutely is and continues to be  relevant right the way through so you  think it does matter to have  single sex provision for girls each  school every school has to work out its  own arrangements but it's important to  recognize that we've got so conflicting  rights here this is not something that  you can steamroll and we have to  acknowledge  that some of the gender issues come  directly into conflict with some of the  sex basically amanda would your message  be to schools uh  that have removed single sex spaces  what's your message then that they  shouldn't  my message is that is that they've got  to make sure that the jet that the very  real tensions here have been air  discussed that they've got buy-in for  whatever solution this is we don't  prescribe what school what schools do  when conflicts between rights arise this  is not the first time that we found  ourselves um in a place where we can see  a clear conflict of rights so so much of  my time at ofsted we've been dealing  with places where religious rights and  sex sex rights conflict and we found  illegal segregation or where religion  and sexuality can flip whereas religious  schools don't want to teach about  homosexuality  i've got one quick question for you on  the issue of single sex schools over 50  of teachers in england have said they  have at least one pupil who's identified  as transgender do you still think single  sex schools will exist in a generation's  time or will society have moved on from  that form of demarcation between people  there are certainly far fewer single sex  schools than there once were but  in a world where parent choice matters  i'd be very reluctant  to see a mandate um that there should be  no no single sex schools yes issues of  gender identity um create some  difficulties at the borderline no  question about that um but i certainly  wouldn't be calling to to obamacare  all right well amanda  we've run out of time thank you that was  fascinating

